    {
      "name": "Dimension Line",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "dimension-line",
      "description": "The budget drawn as a dimension line with quotes plotted as diamond markers coloured by verdict.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-dim\"><span class=\"ds-dim-label\">$2,500 – $4,000</span><div class=\"ds-dim-track\"><span class=\"ds-dim-ext\" style=\"left:25%\"></span><span class=\"ds-dim-ext\" style=\"left:70%\"></span><span class=\"ds-dim-base\"></span><span class=\"ds-dim-line\" style=\"left:25%;width:45%\"></span></div><div class=\"ds-dim-plots\"><span class=\"ds-plot ds-within\" style=\"left:52%\"></span><span class=\"ds-plot ds-over\" style=\"left:82%\"></span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-dim{position:relative;max-width:30rem;padding-top:0.25rem;font-family:Chivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-dim-label{display:block;margin-left:47.5%;transform:translateX(-50%);width:max-content;padding:0 0.375rem;background:var(--sheet,#fbfcfe);color:var(--blue,#1a4e9e);font-size:0.875rem;font-weight:600;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-dim-track{position:relative;height:1.25rem}.ds-dim-ext{position:absolute;top:-1rem;bottom:-6px;width:1px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--blue,#1a4e9e) 60%,transparent)}.ds-dim-base{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:50%;height:1px;background:var(--rule,#c3d2e6)}.ds-dim-line{position:absolute;top:50%;height:1px;background:var(--blue,#1a4e9e);transform-origin:left center;animation:ds-draw 900ms cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1) both}.ds-dim-plots{position:relative;height:1rem}.ds-plot{position:absolute;top:2px;width:8px;height:8px;margin-left:-4px;border:1.5px solid currentColor;background:var(--sheet,#fbfcfe);transform:rotate(45deg)}.ds-within{color:var(--approved,#1e6a45)}.ds-over{color:var(--redline,#b7331c)}@keyframes ds-draw{from{transform:scaleX(0)}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-dim-line{animation:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Drawing Register Row",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "register-row-hover",
      "description": "A list as one sheet: 1.5px ink header rule, hairline rows, whole-row link, tint on hover.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-reg\"><div class=\"ds-reg-head\"><span>Sheet</span><span>Job</span><span class=\"ds-r\">Budget</span></div><a class=\"ds-reg-row\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-reg-no\">No. 7C41E2</span><span class=\"ds-reg-title\">Managed firewall for a dental office</span><span class=\"ds-r ds-reg-money\">$2,500 – $4,000</span></a><a class=\"ds-reg-row\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-reg-no\">No. 3A90F1</span><span class=\"ds-reg-title\">Migrate reporting database</span><span class=\"ds-r ds-reg-money\">Up to $6,000</span></a></div>",
      "css": ".ds-reg{max-width:40rem;background:var(--sheet,#fbfcfe);border:1px solid var(--rule-strong,#7f93b3);font-family:Chivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--ink,#12213a)}.ds-reg-head,.ds-reg-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:6.5rem 1fr 9rem;gap:1.5rem;padding:0.75rem 1.5rem}.ds-reg-head{border-bottom:1.5px solid var(--ink,#12213a);font-size:0.875rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink-2,#475872)}.ds-reg-row{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:1rem;border-top:1px solid var(--rule,#c3d2e6);color:inherit;text-decoration:none;transition:background-color 150ms cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)}.ds-reg-head+.ds-reg-row{border-top:0}.ds-reg-row:hover,.ds-reg-row:focus-visible{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--tint,#e3ecf7) 60%,transparent);outline:none}.ds-reg-row:hover .ds-reg-title,.ds-reg-row:focus-visible .ds-reg-title{color:var(--blue,#1a4e9e);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px}.ds-reg-no{font-family:\"Chivo Mono\",ui-monospace,\"SF Mono\",monospace;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--ink-2,#475872)}.ds-reg-title{font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:700}.ds-r{text-align:right}.ds-reg-money{font-weight:600;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Blueline Spec Sheet",
    "overview": "Every job is an engineering drawing. Pages sit on a faint engineering-grid ground, and the things people act on are drawing sheets: cool white stock framed by a hairline and an inner border, with a ruled title block in the corner holding the sheet number, category and state. The budget is drawn as a dimension line with extension lines and arrowheads, and quotes are plotted against it as markers. Lists are drawing registers: a heavy ink header rule, hairline row dividers, a whole-row link.\n\nThe world is drafted, not decorated. Linework carries structure: 1px rules for division, 1.5px ink rules for anything that holds a record (title blocks, register headers, the category index). Blueprint blue is the drafting pen and the action colour; redline is the checker's pen and marks only what is wrong or refused. Corners are square everywhere. Depth is a sheet lying on a table, not a card floating off a screen.\n\nType is one family, Chivo, in sentence case throughout. Figures that get compared (money, counts) are set in Chivo's tabular figures so columns align; Chivo Mono is reserved for sheet numbers, the one identifier a drawing sets like a drawing number. The system refuses the SaaS hero-plus-card-grid and the uniform rounded shadow card.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Engineering-grid ground (8px fine, 40px major) with drawing sheets laid on it.",
      "Blueprint blue for linework, links and the primary action; redline only for errors, declines, cancellations and over-budget marks.",
      "Square corners, hairline rules, a heavier 1.5px ink rule for record-holding structures.",
      "State shown as a drawing-legend symbol plus its word.",
      "One typeface family; tabular Chivo for money, mono only for sheet numbers.",
      "One motion moment per surface at most: a line that draws, markers that settle."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Drafting Pen Rule",
        "body": "Blue is the pen that draws the sheet and the button that moves a job forward. It does not become a fill for surfaces other than primary buttons, selection, and the single closing blueprint band.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Redline Rule",
        "body": "Redline marks only what is wrong, refused, cancelled or over budget. It is never decoration, never emphasis, never a brand accent.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Measure Rule",
        "body": "Money and counts are set in Chivo with tabular figures (`tnum`); Chivo Mono is used only for sheet numbers. Reason: in the build, mono's comma spacing split amounts apart, and mono on money read as costume rather than as a drawing. Dates are not set in mono either: they render as relative words (\"3 days ago\") in note style inside a `<time>` element, with the full date in its title.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "Every label, column head, title-block label and button is sentence case with default tracking. The world's native all-caps drafting lettering was deliberately not adopted.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper Rule",
        "body": "A sheet may cast one soft drop and nothing else lifts. No hover elevation, no stacked shadows, no hard offset shadows.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do put the things people act on inside a sheet: stock fill, strong outer rule, inner hairline frame 5px in, one soft drop.",
      "Do give every job a title block with its sheet number (mono, \"No. XXXXXX\") and its state mark.",
      "Do draw budgets as a dimension line and plot quotes against it, with the verdict also stated in words.",
      "Do set money and counts in Chivo with tabular figures; keep Chivo Mono for sheet numbers only.",
      "Do show state with a legend symbol plus its word, using the fixed symbol-to-state mapping.",
      "Do use 1px rules to divide and a 1.5px ink rule for record structures (title blocks, register headers, index tables).",
      "Do keep every label, head and button in sentence case with default tracking.",
      "Do keep controls at 44px minimum height (36px for the small button) with the 2px blue focus outline offset 3px."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't round corners on any surface or control; the radius is 0px everywhere.",
      "Don't build a SaaS hero-plus-card-grid or use uniform rounded shadow cards.",
      "Don't set money or dates in Chivo Mono; mono's comma spacing splits amounts and reads as costume.",
      "Don't use redline for anything but errors, declines, cancellations and over-budget marks.",
      "Don't let colour alone carry a state; the symbol and the word must be present.",
      "Don't add shadows beyond the sheet's single soft drop, and never a hard offset shadow.",
      "Don't add small uppercase or tracked labels above headlines.",
      "Don't add more than one motion moment to a surface."
    ]
  }
}